10
00:48:38,181 --> 00:48:44,181
Moana is a 2016 American animated musical adventure film produced by Walt Disney Animation
Studios and directed by John Musker and Ron Clements from a screenplay by Jared Bush.

11
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
It stars Dwayne Johnson and Auliʻi Cravalho in her film debut.

12
00:58:21,818 --> 00:58:27,818
It features songs written by Lin-Manuel Miranda, Opetaia Foaʻi, and Mark
Mancina, and an original score also composed by Mancina.

13
01:03:13,636 --> 01:03:19,636
The film is set in ancient Polynesia and tells the story of Moana, the strong-willed daughter of a chief of a
coastal village, who is chosen by the ocean itself to reunite a mystical relic with the goddess Te Fiti.

14
01:08:05,454 --> 01:08:11,454
When a blight strikes her island, Moana sets sail in search of Maui, a legendary
demigod, in hopes of returning the relic to Te Fiti and saving her people.

15
01:12:57,272 --> 01:13:03,272
The screenplay takes inspiration from Polynesian myths.

16
01:17:49,090 --> 01:17:55,090
Moana premiered during the AFI Fest at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on November
14, 2016, and was released theatrically in the United States on November 23.

17
01:22:40,909 --> 01:22:46,909
The film received positive reviews from critics and was a
commercial success, grossing $687 million worldwide.

18
01:27:32,727 --> 01:27:38,727
At the 89th Academy Awards, the film received two nominations for Best
Animated Feature and Best Original Song ("How Far I'll Go").

19
01:32:24,545 --> 01:32:30,545
Available on Disney+, Moana was the most-streamed film in the United States from 2020 to 2024, leading The Wall Street Journal to describe it as "the
No.1 movie in streaming history." A sequel, Moana 2, was released in 2024, while a live-action remake is scheduled for release in 2026.

20
01:37:16,363 --> 01:37:22,363
The film explores themes of sailboat, sea, island, saving the world, ocean.

21
01:42:08,181 --> 01:42:14,181
The tone is lighthearted.
